<title>FRANCE: Danone could sell glass unit - paper.</title>
<headline>Danone could sell glass unit - paper.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>French food group Danone is studying the sale of its glass packaging unit and the operation could take place in the next few months, the Le Monde newspaper said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The newspaper, quoting industry sources, said Owens Illinois of the United States was best placed to buy the unit.</p>
<p>There was no immediate comment at Danone.</p>
<p>Le Monde said financial analysts put a value of eight billion francs on the unit with annual sales of 6.3 billion and an operating income of 700 million.</p>
</text>
